From: q2q port
Subject: [PATCH] q2q: present the iPhone X display on panels larger in one dimension

The Galaxy Z Fold3 inner panel is 2208x1768 (native landscape scan). ios-sweet only
presented 1125x2436 when the panel was smaller in both dimensions, so iOS saw the raw
panel and backboardd kept asking for AppleM2ScalerCSCDriver. Present 1125x2436 whenever
sweetfb_native is not set; the swap copy clips on all edges (centered, cropped 334 rows
top and bottom on q2q).

Boot-args sweetfb_lw / sweetfb_lh (2026-11-23) present another logical size instead, to
try filling the inner panel (e.g. 1768x2208) without a kernel rebuild.

---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -170,9 +170,19 @@
 	PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetfb_native", &native, sizeof(native));
 	fLogicalW = fWidth;
 	fLogicalH = fHeight;
-	if (!native && fWidth <= SWEET_FB_LOGICAL_W && fHeight <= SWEET_FB_LOGICAL_H) {
+	if (!native) { /* q2q: also when the panel is larger in one dimension; the swap copy clips */
 		fLogicalW = SWEET_FB_LOGICAL_W;
 		fLogicalH = SWEET_FB_LOGICAL_H;
 	}
+	{
+		/* q2q: sweetfb_lw / sweetfb_lh present another logical display size */
+		uint32_t q2q_lw = 0, q2q_lh = 0;
+		(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetfb_lw", &q2q_lw, sizeof(q2q_lw));
+		(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetfb_lh", &q2q_lh, sizeof(q2q_lh));
+		if (q2q_lw >= 320 && q2q_lw <= 4000 && q2q_lh >= 320 && q2q_lh <= 4000) {
+			fLogicalW = q2q_lw;
+			fLogicalH = q2q_lh;
+		}
+	}
 	fOffX = (int32_t)(fLogicalW - fWidth) / 2;
 	fOffY = (int32_t)(fLogicalH - fHeight) / 2;
